1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:01,665
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,666 --> 00:00:03,041
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:05,249
(Episode 41)

4
00:00:07,316 --> 00:00:09,217
Hey, don't cry.

5
00:00:09,666 --> 00:00:11,958
You're going to make me cry too.

6
00:00:12,791 --> 00:00:18,125
It's not fair. I'm so upset.

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:21,708
- Tae O.
- Yeah?

8
00:00:21,958 --> 00:00:26,500
They say the world rewards hard work.
That's not true, right?

9
00:00:26,989 --> 00:00:29,823
I guess we got our children's book wrong.

10
00:00:30,416 --> 00:00:33,581
In this world, your connections,
your background, your parents.

11
00:00:34,009 --> 00:00:36,625
Those things matter more, right?

12
00:00:37,656 --> 00:00:40,730
I'm sorry. I was wrong. I admit it.

13
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:43,833
Be quiet.

14
00:00:44,422 --> 00:00:47,463
Why are you still sitting there?
I can't even stand looking at you.

15
00:00:47,625 --> 00:00:49,625
Ji Ni.

16
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:51,250
Ji Hu...

17
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,875
I have a lot to say too.

18
00:00:54,357 --> 00:00:55,399
Like what?

19
00:00:55,642 --> 00:00:57,041
That you had no choice?

20
00:00:57,708 --> 00:00:59,958
That's just cowardly.

21
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:03,041
What? He only protects his own family?

22
00:01:04,458 --> 00:01:05,721
Good for you.

23
00:01:05,958 --> 00:01:07,831
That's just selfishness.

24
00:01:08,208 --> 00:01:09,917
Is his family the only one that matters?

25
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:12,125
Does that give him the right
to insult someone else's family?

26
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:14,375
I'm sorry.

27
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:21,125
Who do you think you are,
making my mom cry like this?

28
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:25,416
The only person who has the right
to criticize my mom is Yeong Ju.

29
00:01:25,833 --> 00:01:28,000
So don't go throwing stones at her
like that.

30
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:29,375
Ji Ni.

31
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:33,045
You've seen Do Hee's drawings, right?

32
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:35,207
There's not an ounce of creativity
in them.

33
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:36,827
They're just drawings
she learned at an art academy.

34
00:01:37,541 --> 00:01:38,875
She draws them all the same.

35
00:01:39,541 --> 00:01:40,873
You call that good?

36
00:01:44,364 --> 00:01:47,506
What are you doing here like you've done
nothing wrong? You two broke up?

37
00:01:47,791 --> 00:01:49,583
What does that have to do with me?

38
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:51,291
Get out.

39
00:01:51,458 --> 00:01:53,616
- I don't accept your apology.
- Seriously...

40
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:57,541
What? Get out now.

41
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:05,250
- Ji Hu.
- Are you leaving?

42
00:02:06,458 --> 00:02:09,291
So what, are we done for today?

43
00:02:10,708 --> 00:02:14,008
No. We should drink.

44
00:02:15,375 --> 00:02:17,226
Come on. Cheers.

45
00:02:18,666 --> 00:02:20,625
- Yeah.
- Let's drink till we drop.

46
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:22,375
Cheers!

47
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:51,648
Stop drinking.

48
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,791
I'm not drunk.

49
00:02:55,906 --> 00:02:57,401
I want to get drunk, though.

50
00:02:58,458 --> 00:03:01,155
I can't stop thinking
about how my mom looked when she cried.

51
00:03:04,625 --> 00:03:09,291
Why was I even born if all I do...

52
00:03:09,458 --> 00:03:11,450
is make my mom suffer like this?

53
00:03:14,144 --> 00:03:15,685
There's some left
in the fridge downstairs, right?

54
00:03:16,414 --> 00:03:17,717
I'll get it.

55
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:20,833
I'll get it, Tae O.

56
00:03:23,291 --> 00:03:25,166
Get something to cover Jung A with.

57
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:29,208
I'll get some ice cream too.

58
00:03:39,458 --> 00:03:41,375
You're here.

59
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:43,708
Ms. Big Shot.

60
00:03:46,956 --> 00:03:48,040
You've been here?

61
00:03:48,958 --> 00:03:50,416
You kicked me out.

62
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:56,010
Must be nice to be able
to take your mom's side.

63
00:03:58,083 --> 00:03:59,416
I don't have anyone.

64
00:04:00,798 --> 00:04:05,382
My parents have lived their whole lives
by the military code.

65
00:04:06,375 --> 00:04:07,625
How could I ever badmouth them?

66
00:04:08,083 --> 00:04:09,416
Do whatever you want.

67
00:04:13,958 --> 00:04:17,833
Don't make a scene here. Go home.

68
00:04:19,833 --> 00:04:21,083
Are you telling me to leave again?

69
00:04:22,351 --> 00:04:24,351
You're so cruel.

70
00:04:25,583 --> 00:04:28,166
I thought we had something in common.

71
00:04:30,958 --> 00:04:32,666
When I saw you...

72
00:04:34,208 --> 00:04:37,916
donating bone marrow to that little kid,

73
00:04:40,622 --> 00:04:42,554
I wanted to tell you...

74
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:48,333
what it's like to always live
in your parents' shadow.

75
00:04:49,916 --> 00:04:51,708
I thought you'd understand.

76
00:04:54,083 --> 00:04:55,114
What are you talking about?

77
00:04:56,958 --> 00:05:00,590
Prince, stop acting like a spoiled brat
and go home.

78
00:05:01,083 --> 00:05:03,208
Just go home, okay?

79
00:05:03,458 --> 00:05:05,041
I'm not a prince.

80
00:05:06,671 --> 00:05:09,754
I'm a princess. The Little Mermaid.

81
00:05:11,393 --> 00:05:13,685
Do you know how the Little Mermaid feels?

82
00:05:15,502 --> 00:05:16,706
"The Little Mermaid?"

83
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,375
I'm asking if you know
the pain in my soul.

84
00:05:21,456 --> 00:05:24,290
And you're the one being rude. Seriously?

85
00:05:30,768 --> 00:05:32,935
Are you okay? Get up.

86
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:41,320
No.

87
00:05:43,288 --> 00:05:45,341
I'm seriously losing my mind.

88
00:05:46,916 --> 00:05:49,416
No one knows.

89
00:06:07,352 --> 00:06:08,352
Na Ji Ni!

90
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:47,625
My head is killing me.

91
00:06:51,541 --> 00:06:52,625
Are you okay?

92
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,416
Yeah. You're here?

93
00:06:58,748 --> 00:07:00,956
Did you clean everything up?
How's your stomach?

94
00:07:01,458 --> 00:07:04,750
My head's throbbing a little,
but I'm okay.

95
00:07:05,875 --> 00:07:07,166
Na Ji Ni, you really...

96
00:07:07,851 --> 00:07:08,935
But what about Ji Hu?

97
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:15,208
He said he can't sleep anywhere
but his own bed, so he took a taxi home.

98
00:07:15,989 --> 00:07:18,073
Well, that's just how he is.

99
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:19,791
Jung A.

100
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:22,166
Didn't you say you had a meeting today?

101
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:24,375
Right.

102
00:07:25,083 --> 00:07:26,665
Hurry up and shower. You're all puffy.

103
00:07:26,666 --> 00:07:28,625
Fix your hair and make yourself
look pretty before you go.

104
00:07:28,666 --> 00:07:30,000
Okay.

105
00:07:30,041 --> 00:07:31,291
Thanks so much, girl.

106
00:07:31,375 --> 00:07:33,541
I'll make it up to you when I get famous.

107
00:08:02,016 --> 00:08:06,096
You spent the night out without even
telling me? And you turned off your phone?

108
00:08:08,583 --> 00:08:11,583
I'm sorry. I was drinking
with Jung A at the cafe.

109
00:08:11,625 --> 00:08:13,333
Hey, are you acting like this
because you don't have a dad?

110
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,375
What does not having a dad
have to do with this?

111
00:08:15,416 --> 00:08:18,500
Kids with dads don't spend the night out
without permission.

112
00:08:18,889 --> 00:08:20,499
You're looking down on me
because I'm all you have?

113
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,875
Unbelievable!

114
00:08:22,166 --> 00:08:24,875
Everyone I drank with last night
has a dad.

115
00:08:25,041 --> 00:08:27,666
Besides Jung A, who else
were you drinking with?

116
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:29,333
Are you dating someone?

117
00:08:29,375 --> 00:08:31,333
Your voice is ringing in my head.
Stop talking.

118
00:08:31,583 --> 00:08:33,000
I'm not dating anyone, so don't worry.

119
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:35,125
As if I'd date someone.

120
00:08:35,166 --> 00:08:36,833
You should date someone.

121
00:08:36,958 --> 00:08:38,166
Then I'd understand.

122
00:08:38,766 --> 00:08:42,208
I don't want a love like yours
or a love like Dad's. I'm not doing it.

123
00:08:42,458 --> 00:08:44,207
I'm going to live like this
and die like this.

124
00:08:44,208 --> 00:08:45,875
You little brat!

125
00:08:46,375 --> 00:08:49,148
Hey, Mai left home.

126
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:51,208
If you're staying here,
at least be considerate of Yeong Ju.

127
00:08:51,291 --> 00:08:53,375
Really? Where did she go?

128
00:08:53,458 --> 00:08:55,750
If I knew where she was, that wouldn't
be leaving home. She'd just be out.

129
00:08:56,625 --> 00:08:57,791
You little brat.

130
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,291
Seriously!

131
00:09:05,666 --> 00:09:07,666
This is exhausting.

132
00:09:11,791 --> 00:09:14,666
I really need to cut back on drinking.
This is killing me.

133
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:24,791
Please help me out.

134
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,082
Na Ji Ni, help my uncle get married.

135
00:09:28,083 --> 00:09:31,500
Why? You're not cute at all.

136
00:09:31,875 --> 00:09:33,625
He's ridiculously tall and lanky.

137
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:36,416
"Not cute?" Then...

138
00:09:40,458 --> 00:09:42,958
Please help me. Okay?

139
00:09:46,791 --> 00:09:48,708
Fine. Enough already.

140
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,375
I'm rooting for Yeong Ju
to get married too.

141
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,541
Really?

142
00:09:59,416 --> 00:10:00,750
Here's my plan.

143
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:05,965
I'll collect photos of the two of them
and make a video. What do you think?

144
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:10,166
If you have a better idea, let me know.

145
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:12,291
Sounds good.

146
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:17,125
I'll draw on the photos.

147
00:10:18,458 --> 00:10:20,541
Your drawings are the best.

148
00:10:22,024 --> 00:10:23,124
I should see for myself.

149
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:25,916
Your drawings have soul.

150
00:10:26,583 --> 00:10:29,414
They're sad, but they're strong.

151
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:33,041
Why are you talking so casually?

152
00:10:33,530 --> 00:10:35,947
You're younger than me.

153
00:10:36,333 --> 00:10:39,041
Watch it, you little punk.

154
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:43,778
This is great.

155
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:51,666
My uncle's going to love this.

156
00:11:01,708 --> 00:11:04,833
Seriously, he's such a weird person.

157
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:17,793
Your mom was up all night,
waiting for you to come home.

158
00:11:18,083 --> 00:11:19,573
Don't do that again.

159
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:22,583
No matter how much you drink,
staying out all night isn't okay.

160
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:25,791
Okay.

161
00:11:26,541 --> 00:11:29,166
By the way, I heard about Mai.

162
00:11:29,541 --> 00:11:31,208
You must be upset.

163
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,041
Yeah.

164
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:35,708
I'll take care of that.

165
00:11:36,041 --> 00:11:37,041
Why?

166
00:11:37,875 --> 00:11:41,791
I already feel bad enough living off you,
so at least let me do this.

167
00:11:43,916 --> 00:11:46,625
Your mom gives me living expenses,
so don't say things like that.

168
00:11:46,791 --> 00:11:48,166
And don't feel like you're a burden.

169
00:11:48,421 --> 00:11:51,208
- Mom does?
- You really don't know your mom at all.

170
00:11:53,958 --> 00:11:55,041
Have a seat.

171
00:11:55,666 --> 00:11:56,666
Okay.

172
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:05,585
I noticed you were pretty harsh
with her last time too.

173
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:06,833
Don't do that.

174
00:12:07,291 --> 00:12:09,208
Being a parent doesn't
make you invulnerable.

175
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:12,166
Your words can really hurt them.

176
00:12:14,375 --> 00:12:15,375
Okay.

177
00:12:15,666 --> 00:12:18,500
I heard you got fired.
Is that why you were drinking?

178
00:12:19,875 --> 00:12:21,208
That was part of it.

179
00:12:21,541 --> 00:12:26,458
I don't know who hurt her,
but she came home crying.

180
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:32,163
She said you'd always struggled
because I didn't do the paperwork sooner.

181
00:12:32,166 --> 00:12:33,875
Why is that your fault?

182
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,666
- It's all because of her.
- There you go again.

183
00:12:36,125 --> 00:12:37,375
You're talking like that again.

184
00:12:37,916 --> 00:12:40,500
Other people may say that,
but you shouldn't.

185
00:12:40,672 --> 00:12:42,839
Who else could your mom
have done this for?

186
00:12:43,833 --> 00:12:44,875
I know.

187
00:12:45,625 --> 00:12:47,333
It's all because of me.

188
00:12:49,458 --> 00:12:52,000
You must hate me.

189
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,916
No, it's okay.

190
00:12:56,004 --> 00:12:57,688
You're just like Seung Hyun.

191
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:01,416
You say you're okay,
but you're hurting inside.

192
00:13:02,125 --> 00:13:03,320
Parents can tell.

193
00:13:05,833 --> 00:13:06,833
Yeah.

194
00:13:07,666 --> 00:13:09,438
I'm the one who should be sorry...

195
00:13:10,875 --> 00:13:12,848
- for being born.
- Don't ever say that.

196
00:13:14,166 --> 00:13:18,083
When you keep talking like this,
your mom can't help but worry.

197
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:21,000
No one is born for no reason.

198
00:13:26,541 --> 00:13:27,617
I'm sorry.

199
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:31,684
What are you sorry for?

200
00:13:32,083 --> 00:13:34,859
I should've only been angry with your mom,

201
00:13:35,958 --> 00:13:38,125
but I said some pretty harsh things
to you too.

202
00:13:38,583 --> 00:13:40,048
I know I hurt you.

203
00:13:43,875 --> 00:13:45,125
That's between the adults.

204
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:46,920
It's all in the past.

205
00:13:47,750 --> 00:13:50,208
You kids just live your own lives.

206
00:13:51,796 --> 00:13:55,129
I hope my children can do the same.

207
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:03,138
I've failed you...

208
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:07,253
and put you through
a lot of difficult times.

209
00:14:08,958 --> 00:14:10,166
I'm truly sorry.

210
00:14:12,416 --> 00:14:13,416
No, it's okay.

211
00:14:54,666 --> 00:14:55,666
What about Ji Hu?

212
00:14:56,833 --> 00:14:59,231
He came home completely drunk
in the early hours of the morning.

213
00:15:00,386 --> 00:15:03,011
Then why did he even say
he was breaking up with Do Hee?

214
00:15:03,208 --> 00:15:04,625
I don't like it one bit.

215
00:15:05,333 --> 00:15:06,931
I'm the only man you need.

216
00:15:07,041 --> 00:15:08,458
Forget about Ji Hu now.

217
00:15:09,458 --> 00:15:10,791
Seriously.

218
00:15:11,833 --> 00:15:13,100
I can't eat breakfast.

219
00:15:13,416 --> 00:15:14,958
Sit down. At least have some soup.

220
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:16,666
Don't make my woman worry about you.

221
00:15:17,048 --> 00:15:18,048
What?

222
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,083
Sit down.

223
00:15:21,750 --> 00:15:23,500
- I'll just have some soup and go.
- Okay.

224
00:15:24,541 --> 00:15:25,666
Who did you drink with?

225
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:27,208
I heard you were completely wasted.

226
00:15:27,583 --> 00:15:28,683
I drank with Tae O.

227
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:30,666
Hey, don't worry.

228
00:15:31,125 --> 00:15:33,457
Do Hee has no intention
of breaking up with you.

229
00:15:33,666 --> 00:15:35,541
She probably hasn't told
the Ambassador either.

230
00:15:35,666 --> 00:15:37,541
Mom, I broke up with her.

231
00:15:37,625 --> 00:15:39,333
- What?
- Who said you could break up with her?

232
00:15:39,625 --> 00:15:42,125
You may have started dating on your own,
but now everything is intertwined.

233
00:15:42,166 --> 00:15:43,923
You think you can just end it
because you want to?

234
00:15:44,916 --> 00:15:47,458
Once a man decides, that's it.
Why are you going back on it?

235
00:15:47,541 --> 00:15:48,899
So I'm supposed to protect only my family?

236
00:15:49,291 --> 00:15:52,125
- By that logic, Do Hee isn't my family.
- What?

237
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,041
I'm sorry.

238
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:56,574
But if I don't break up with her now,
I think I'll regret it forever.

239
00:15:57,333 --> 00:15:58,583
I'm not changing my mind.

240
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,750
Hey, you...

241
00:16:02,875 --> 00:16:04,625
That's not like him at all.

242
00:16:04,791 --> 00:16:05,875
Excuse me.

243
00:16:08,083 --> 00:16:10,250
Hey, Ji Hu.

244
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:12,375
What?

245
00:16:12,583 --> 00:16:14,333
Is everything going well
with the proposal preparations?

246
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:18,540
Is that all you ever think about?

247
00:16:18,541 --> 00:16:19,833
Of course. What else would I think about?

248
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:22,125
Got it, so don't worry.

249
00:16:23,041 --> 00:16:24,884
Thanks. Love you.

250
00:16:25,166 --> 00:16:27,333
You know I love you, right? I love you.

251
00:16:33,587 --> 00:16:36,504
Tae O, how much did you two drink?

252
00:16:36,708 --> 00:16:39,000
Yes, sir. We'll be more careful.

253
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,500
It's Do Hee's first day at work,
so take good care of her.

254
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,333
Of course.

255
00:16:48,458 --> 00:16:49,708
Good morning.

256
00:16:50,916 --> 00:16:53,875
What is this?
Did you come here to work, or...

257
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,083
are you here for a fashion show?

258
00:16:56,291 --> 00:16:57,623
I came here to work.

259
00:16:57,791 --> 00:16:59,765
Do the employees here all speak casually
to each other?

260
00:17:00,458 --> 00:17:03,833
Anyway, that's your desk.

261
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,125
I know.

262
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:16,305
When was the last time
you dusted this place?

263
00:17:16,375 --> 00:17:18,541
You can dust it yourself
before you use it.

264
00:17:18,583 --> 00:17:21,768
I could've fired you, but I let it slide.
Why don't you show some gratitude?

265
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:24,208
And you just barged
into someone else's home.

266
00:17:24,416 --> 00:17:27,903
I forgave you for something unforgivable,
so you better treat me well.

267
00:17:28,574 --> 00:17:30,743
I heard you're required to work here
for three years.

268
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,541
Thank you, Ms. Do.

269
00:17:39,583 --> 00:17:41,239
I want a morning coffee.

270
00:17:41,291 --> 00:17:42,333
Have one.

271
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:45,958
I sent you the files
you need to review today.

272
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:48,500
Check them, and make sure
you finish the color work.

273
00:17:48,708 --> 00:17:51,670
What? Not instant coffee.

274
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,151
I'll drink it if you bring me
an iced Americano.

275
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:56,458
Why would I get you an iced Americano?

276
00:17:57,250 --> 00:17:58,500
I'm on my way.

277
00:18:12,583 --> 00:18:14,720
Yes. You're on standby, right?

278
00:18:15,416 --> 00:18:16,500
I'll send the file.

279
00:18:27,136 --> 00:18:28,136
General.

280
00:18:29,833 --> 00:18:31,583
Have you found the woman
Sa Bin has been seeing?

281
00:18:31,875 --> 00:18:32,875
I'm sorry.

282
00:18:33,083 --> 00:18:36,574
I kept watch in the parking lot,
but he stayed at the clinic,

283
00:18:36,625 --> 00:18:39,708
except when he went out
for an off-site consultation.

284
00:18:39,922 --> 00:18:42,130
Where did he go? Did you follow him?

285
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,916
- No.
- Stay on him.

286
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Yes, sir.

287
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:53,875
General, I feel like you and I
have become the Cupids of this family.

288
00:18:55,291 --> 00:18:57,083
I'd rather be out at sea.

289
00:18:57,125 --> 00:18:59,375
- Being Cupid is exhausting.
- Exactly.

290
00:19:00,041 --> 00:19:01,041
At your service.

291
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,625
Are you comfortable?

292
00:19:13,791 --> 00:19:14,916
Yes, it feels good.

293
00:19:16,125 --> 00:19:18,166
Doctor, I'm here.

294
00:19:18,333 --> 00:19:20,708
- You're here? Come in.
- Yes.

295
00:19:31,916 --> 00:19:34,875
- Give me your hand.
- Why again?

296
00:19:34,916 --> 00:19:36,165
Hurry up.

297
00:19:36,166 --> 00:19:39,125
Seriously.

298
00:19:42,416 --> 00:19:45,242
- I'm starting now.
- Okay.

299
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:50,332
I didn't come yesterday.

300
00:19:50,333 --> 00:19:51,541
I waited all day.

301
00:20:03,208 --> 00:20:04,583
Now, open and close your hand.

302
00:20:04,833 --> 00:20:07,707
That's it. You need to do this often.

303
00:20:07,708 --> 00:20:09,166
Now raise your arm.

304
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,125
A little higher.

305
00:20:12,791 --> 00:20:14,708
It's gotten much better with treatment.

306
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:17,208
Good. With frozen shoulder,
you need to come in regularly.

307
00:21:02,416 --> 00:21:05,208
It's been ages since I sent the file.
Why haven't you sent it yet?

308
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,666
Hurry up.

309
00:21:10,625 --> 00:21:14,000
Why do I keep losing followers?
This is driving me crazy.

310
00:21:28,166 --> 00:21:29,833
What happened to my face?

311
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:37,879
Don't draw on the face.
Please work on the coloring, Ms. Do.

312
00:21:38,291 --> 00:21:40,333
I'm almost done, so just wait.

313
00:21:40,922 --> 00:21:41,922
(Secret Talk, Alternate Account,
Coloring File.png sent by unknown user)

314
00:21:47,166 --> 00:21:48,208
Well done.

315
00:21:53,125 --> 00:21:54,666
I sent it. Check it.

316
00:22:03,291 --> 00:22:04,958
What on earth...

317
00:22:05,375 --> 00:22:07,583
I studied abroad, you know.
Don't underestimate me.

318
00:22:07,958 --> 00:22:09,125
I did better than Na Ji Ni, right?

319
00:22:09,166 --> 00:22:11,003
Why are you so hung up on Na Ji Ni?

320
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:14,040
Do Hee is Do Hee, and Ji Ni is Ji Ni.
Isn't that how it is?

321
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:15,291
You don't understand.

322
00:22:16,291 --> 00:22:18,512
You don't know what middle school
was like for me because of her.

323
00:22:19,166 --> 00:22:22,875
I can never live under the same sky
or breathe the same air as her.

324
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:24,833
Then what?

325
00:22:25,041 --> 00:22:26,416
I'll leave that to your imagination.

326
00:22:29,833 --> 00:22:31,228
I have an interview this afternoon.

327
00:22:31,625 --> 00:22:33,083
It's okay if I leave work
a little early, right?

328
00:22:44,166 --> 00:22:45,333
Na Ji Ni.

329
00:22:46,833 --> 00:22:47,833
Yes.

330
00:22:47,958 --> 00:22:49,958
You remember our promise yesterday, right?
The proposal.

331
00:22:51,041 --> 00:22:52,041
Yeah.

332
00:22:52,416 --> 00:22:53,624
That's a relief.

333
00:22:53,916 --> 00:22:55,833
I was worried you'd forgotten
because you were drunk.

334
00:22:56,916 --> 00:22:58,812
I think you're the one who forgot.

335
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:01,665
I told you I was rooting for them.

336
00:23:01,666 --> 00:23:02,791
Did you?

337
00:23:03,541 --> 00:23:04,976
You're right. I was a little drunk.

338
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:06,958
You're perfectly fine, Ji Ni.

339
00:23:07,375 --> 00:23:08,680
I process alcohol quickly.

340
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,750
It's my favorite gene
I inherited from my mom.

341
00:23:13,333 --> 00:23:14,671
What can I get you?

342
00:23:14,916 --> 00:23:16,291
You didn't order at the kiosk.

343
00:23:16,333 --> 00:23:17,875
An iced Americano, please.

344
00:23:18,291 --> 00:23:19,291
Okay.

345
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,971
Why are you here alone? Where's Jung A?

346
00:23:31,791 --> 00:23:34,267
She went to a meeting.

347
00:23:34,375 --> 00:23:36,041
She got an offer to appear
on a dating show.

348
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:38,791
She mentioned that yesterday too.

349
00:23:40,083 --> 00:23:42,221
No, she didn't say anything like that
while I was there.

350
00:23:43,041 --> 00:23:44,583
So she waited until I was kicked out
to tell you.

351
00:23:46,728 --> 00:23:47,833
You really hold a grudge.

352
00:23:56,125 --> 00:23:57,375
Here you go.

353
00:23:58,208 --> 00:23:59,416
Thank you.

354
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:22,625
First of all, thanks for coming.

355
00:24:24,066 --> 00:24:25,816
Thank you for inviting me.

356
00:24:27,041 --> 00:24:29,098
I've seen you at the cafe a few times.

357
00:24:29,666 --> 00:24:31,125
I'm a friend of Ji Ni's.

358
00:24:33,125 --> 00:24:34,125
Yes.

359
00:24:35,375 --> 00:24:37,166
You're really handsome.

360
00:24:37,833 --> 00:24:38,833
Right?

361
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:41,416
He'd be perfect
as our surprise cast member, right?

362
00:24:42,541 --> 00:24:44,414
Hey, come on...

363
00:24:45,541 --> 00:24:46,750
Don't get so worked up.

364
00:24:47,958 --> 00:24:51,166
Anyway, what we're looking for in you...

365
00:24:51,416 --> 00:24:54,541
is a warm, caring art teacher type.

366
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,875
Warm and caring.

367
00:24:57,875 --> 00:24:59,708
That sounds like me.

368
00:25:00,685 --> 00:25:04,143
This is a great opportunity, but...

369
00:25:04,166 --> 00:25:06,938
I'm not sure if I should really do it.

370
00:25:07,708 --> 00:25:10,125
I just graduated,
so I'm not sure what's next.

371
00:25:10,416 --> 00:25:13,291
Part of me thinks
I should just open an art academy.

372
00:25:13,833 --> 00:25:16,875
If you appear on the show
and get your face and name out there,

373
00:25:17,166 --> 00:25:19,291
it'd help promote the academy too.
So it'd be even better.

374
00:25:20,041 --> 00:25:23,027
You have to seize an opportunity
when you get one, right?

375
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:40,634
Mom, I told you I want to do it.

376
00:25:41,958 --> 00:25:44,584
You get to decide my art
and my marriage. What about me?

377
00:25:45,041 --> 00:25:46,125
I'm doing this.

378
00:25:46,375 --> 00:25:48,079
I'm confident I can become really famous.

379
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:52,291
Fine, I won't do it. I said I won't.

380
00:25:53,125 --> 00:25:54,166
Don't come to Korea.

381
00:25:54,916 --> 00:25:56,194
I won't do it, so don't come.

382
00:26:07,192 --> 00:26:09,901
I've already transferred the money,
and this is a bonus.

383
00:26:09,958 --> 00:26:11,958
Our sales went up a lot thanks to you.

384
00:26:12,666 --> 00:26:14,666
Thank you.

385
00:26:15,083 --> 00:26:17,583
It's because you have such a good eye.

386
00:26:17,666 --> 00:26:19,416
This dress is really pretty.

387
00:26:19,458 --> 00:26:20,500
Thank you.

388
00:26:20,833 --> 00:26:23,250
Promise me
you won't go work anywhere else.

389
00:26:23,291 --> 00:26:24,750
Don't worry.

390
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:26,916
Loyalty has gotten me into trouble before.

391
00:26:29,073 --> 00:26:32,540
Even when you think things
have gone wrong,

392
00:26:32,541 --> 00:26:35,291
you know how there are people
who stick with it out of loyalty?

393
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:40,810
Think about walking
in our fashion show this fall.

394
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:44,125
I'm serious. Please.

395
00:26:44,833 --> 00:26:46,625
My daughter won't like it.

396
00:26:46,958 --> 00:26:49,625
Don't get your hopes up.
I'll just keep selling clothes.

397
00:26:51,504 --> 00:26:53,004
Then I'll count on you today too.

398
00:26:53,333 --> 00:26:55,166
Yes, thank you.

399
00:27:16,125 --> 00:27:17,833
Welcome. What are you looking for?

400
00:27:18,824 --> 00:27:19,875
Well...

401
00:27:50,166 --> 00:27:53,457
(Family Register)

402
00:27:53,458 --> 00:27:55,083
A caring husband, I see.

403
00:27:55,125 --> 00:27:57,125
If you like it, come back anytime.

404
00:27:57,166 --> 00:27:59,000
You're exactly the character
we've been looking for.

405
00:27:59,041 --> 00:28:01,332
- You're the star of this show.
- "The star?"

406
00:28:01,333 --> 00:28:03,916
You think you're the only family she has?
Mai is family to me too.

407
00:28:03,958 --> 00:28:05,457
I came to apologize.

408
00:28:05,458 --> 00:28:06,458
I'm not accepting your apology.

409
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:08,750
Why are you going this far?
I'm nobody to you.

410
00:28:08,833 --> 00:28:11,875
Because I've finally found
my other half in you.

411
00:28:13,819 --> 00:28:15,819
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
